---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title={`Terms · ${site.name}`} description={`The terms for using ${site.name}.`}>
  <article class="container prose">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated November 2026</p>
    <p>
      {site.name} is free, open-source software for playing audiobooks and podcasts. By using the
      app, the web app or our services, you agree to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content and your add-ons</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        {site.name} is a player. We don’t host, index or link to audio, and we don’t list or
        recommend add-ons made by others.
      </li>
      <li>
        You choose which add-ons to install and what to play. Only play content you have the right
        to, and follow the terms of the services your add-ons connect to.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We run the web app, our own add-ons, a feed and cover proxy, and optional sync for free. We
        may change, limit or stop them, and we will try to give notice first.
      </li>
      <li>
        Don’t abuse them: no automated scraping, no attempts to break them, no use as a general
        proxy.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we
      are not liable for lost data, lost progress or any other damage from using it. Keep your own
      copies of files that matter to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Copyright complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe something on our sites, in our repositories or in one of our own add-ons
      infringes your rights, write to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.copyrightEmail}`}>{site.copyrightEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The code</h2>
    <p>
      The source code is published under the license in the <a href={site.repoUrl}>repository</a>.
      That license, not these terms, governs what you may do with the code.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
